1
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:42,960
Something will work out, I'm sure.

2
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,880
Anyone without a job, come to me.

3
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:04,520
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

4
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:12,000
Look, even Akaneru is burning up.

5
00:01:13,540 --> 00:01:18,260
Somehow, it'll all work out eventually.

6
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:23,540
You get it, right? I get it, I get it.

7
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:27,360
Once you understand, shut up and follow me.

8
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:48,240
I'm Developmental Unit 004, a robot police officer built by the
Metropolitan Police Department with all its combined strength.

9
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:54,780
I was assigned to the Kameari Park police box,
but everything I do is a blunder.

10
00:01:55,260 --> 00:02:02,080
I've been a constant bother to Senior Ryotsu, the god,
and the name they gave me is totally Dame-Tarō.

11
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:08,540
But the god worked hard for me,
a defective unit,

12
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:11,900
and I somehow managed
to avoid being scrapped.

13
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:14,220
Thank you, god.

14
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:17,980
They say a new robot police
officer is being developed too.

15
00:02:18,420 --> 00:02:19,540
I'll do my best too.

16
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:24,700
The flaming robot police officer.

17
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:30,140
Here you go.

18
00:02:32,080 --> 00:02:32,220
Dame-Tarō

19
00:02:32,220 --> 00:02:33,000
No, not at all.

20
00:02:33,460 --> 00:02:36,040
Sorry, that was my job to do.

21
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:40,400
No, no, it's only natural
for a robot to help humans.

22
00:02:40,900 --> 00:02:44,360
But I'm really grateful
Dame-Tarō came to help.

23
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:49,080
Since Terai-san suddenly has
to take time off with mumps,

24
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:53,080
please look after things
until Terai-san comes back.

25
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:54,960
Yes, I'd be happy to.

26
00:02:58,980 --> 00:03:00,920
Looks like our senior officer is back.

27
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:02,920
Alright!

28
00:03:05,740 --> 00:03:06,840
Y-you are?

29
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:09,540
I'm Robot Police Development Unit 005.

30
00:03:09,540 --> 00:03:10,640
Got a problem with that?

31
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:13,000
N-no, no problem.

32
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:17,360
I came because I heard Robot
Police Development Unit 004 is here.

33
00:03:17,360 --> 00:03:25,760
That's you, isn't it? Unit 004?

34
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:28,300
Yes, that's me. Nice to meet you.

35
00:03:28,900 --> 00:03:31,120
A robot like you doesn't
get to talk like that!

36
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:33,600
But I'm the junior here.

37
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:34,620
Listen up.

38
00:03:34,880 --> 00:03:37,660
Seniority and juniority are
just rules of human society.

39
00:03:37,660 --> 00:03:39,880
In the robot world, it's the opposite.

40
00:03:40,540 --> 00:03:42,280
Look, here's my performance specs.

41
00:03:43,900 --> 00:03:46,740
How about that?
My performance is better than yours, right?

42
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:49,940
Newer robots have more advanced
cutting-edge technology,

43
00:03:49,940 --> 00:03:52,200
so they're superior and more impressive.
Remember that!

44
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:54,960
Y-yes, I see.

45
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:57,800
So that's one way of looking at it.

46
00:04:01,260 --> 00:04:03,760
This bicycle looks like
the senior's, though.

47
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:07,560
It was left abandoned in front of the pachinko parlor up ahead,
so I rode it here.

48
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:10,180
It's obviously police property, after all.

49
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:12,960
Wait, so that means...

50
00:04:12,960 --> 00:04:15,160
It wasn't left abandoned at all -

51
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:17,840
Where is it?! My bicycle!

52
00:04:19,020 --> 00:04:21,739
While I was just playing pachinko for a bit,

53
00:04:21,789 --> 00:04:23,520
who the hell did this?

54
00:04:26,780 --> 00:04:29,440
Damn it, I'll definitely find it!

55
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:32,760
Whoa! My bicycle!

56
00:04:34,140 --> 00:04:36,600
Welcome back, Lord.

57
00:04:37,100 --> 00:04:39,360
Why is this bicycle here?

58
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:42,260
Developmental Unit 005 rode it here.

59
00:04:42,260 --> 00:04:44,880
Developmental Unit 005, you say?

60
00:04:45,480 --> 00:04:46,560
Yeah, that's me.

61
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:48,900
Another robot cop

62
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:52,580
So it's you! The delinquent cop
who was playing pachinko on duty!

63
00:04:54,080 --> 00:04:56,540
I-I was patrolling inside the parlor!

64
00:04:56,540 --> 00:04:58,080
Don't go making moves on your own.

65
00:04:58,080 --> 00:04:59,180
You want to fight?

66
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:01,260
When it comes to strength,
robots are stronger!

67
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:04,760
Damn it!

68
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:07,040
Senpai, violence isn't allowed.

69
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:09,120
I just caught your punch, that's all.

70
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:10,900
How dare you do that to me!

71
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:13,100
Feel the power of a robot!

72
00:05:13,100 --> 00:05:15,140
Ultra Game!

73
00:05:17,440 --> 00:05:18,300
Damn it!

74
00:05:18,300 --> 00:05:19,440
It came off!

75
00:05:19,440 --> 00:05:22,440
All talk, and you're weaker than a human!

76
00:05:25,980 --> 00:05:27,280
There, it's done.

77
00:05:28,260 --> 00:05:29,540
Alright, all set.

78
00:05:29,540 --> 00:05:32,600
Now I won't get caught
off guard by a human again.

79
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:37,220
The only thing you've got going for you against humans is your big mouth,
you know.

80
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:39,020
What did you just say, you?!

81
00:05:39,780 --> 00:05:42,080
There are things you can
say and things you can't!

82
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:44,800
What do you mean,
"big mouth" only? Big mouth only!

83
00:05:50,140 --> 00:05:51,460
Hurry up and turn it off!

84
00:05:51,460 --> 00:05:52,200
Yes.

85
00:05:57,960 --> 00:06:00,160
Your whole mouth is full of foam!

86
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:03,380
You idiot! Are you trying to
set the police box on fire?

87
00:06:03,380 --> 00:06:08,380
When emotions run high,
the wiring short-circuits,

88
00:06:08,380 --> 00:06:12,120
and it says it may ignite
the gasoline fuel, right?

89
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:13,500
What did you say?

90
00:06:14,620 --> 00:06:18,340
So that means if it gets angry,
it catches fire?

91
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:20,100
Yes, that's right.

92
00:06:20,540 --> 00:06:23,120
What a totally defective robot you are!

93
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:25,980
What? Who's a defective robot?

94
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:29,900
A robot whose body bursts into flames in anger is obviously defective,
you idiot!

95
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:33,420
Alright, your name is Fire Robot -

96
00:06:33,420 --> 00:06:35,860
Doikari Ennosuke, and that's final.

97
00:06:36,700 --> 00:06:38,100
Who the hell is Ennosuke?

98
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:40,240
Don't give me some ridiculous name.

99
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:43,060
Ryo-chan, no! You'll make him angry.

100
00:06:43,060 --> 00:06:44,980
Ennosuke-san, please don't get angry either.

101
00:06:45,340 --> 00:06:48,140
What? Are you taking the humans' side too?

102
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:50,920
What's that supposed to mean?

103
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:53,900
I'm just going out on patrol for a bit.

104
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:57,100
You know, robots are vindictive.

105
00:06:57,100 --> 00:06:58,980
They have excellent memories, after all.

106
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:07,520
Damn, those guys make me so mad.

107
00:07:07,520 --> 00:07:10,680
The people here are all good people,
you know.

108
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:14,260
That's why there are robots like you,
bowing and scraping to humans.

109
00:07:14,620 --> 00:07:16,260
They just keep piling it on.

110
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:17,760
But

111
00:07:18,260 --> 00:07:20,660
Robots are superior to humans, you know.

112
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:25,720
When it comes to solving equations and trigonometric functions,
humans can't hold a candle to us.

113
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:29,400
I don't think that's much
use in police work, though.

114
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:33,980
For example, there are plenty
of other areas where we excel.

115
00:07:39,640 --> 00:07:41,920
Understood. Please calm down.

116
00:07:44,860 --> 00:07:46,840
Good morning, Chief.

117
00:07:46,840 --> 00:07:48,300
Good morning.

118
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:50,820
G-good morning.

119
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,920
What's wrong, Chief?

120
00:07:55,960 --> 00:07:58,000
Where's Development Unit 005?

121
00:07:59,740 --> 00:08:02,320
Didn't Development Unit 005 come by?

122
00:08:03,300 --> 00:08:05,620
You mean Doikari Ennosuke?

123
00:08:05,620 --> 00:08:07,820
Doikari Ennosuke?

124
00:08:08,300 --> 00:08:10,220
Ryo-chan named it.

125
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:13,800
He's out on patrol with Dame-Tarō right now.

126
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:16,000
I see.

127
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:20,940
Chief, please don't take on
a defective robot like that.

128
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:23,720
Did he cause trouble again?

129
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:24,580
Again?

130
00:08:26,220 --> 00:08:28,180
Did he do something somewhere else too?

131
00:08:29,460 --> 00:08:31,100
Well, that's

132
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:33,440
So he did, didn't he?

133
00:08:36,300 --> 00:08:40,020
Actually, before coming here,
I barged into the chief's office

134
00:08:42,180 --> 00:08:44,460
and you expect us to make them
work without paying a salary?

135
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:47,080
Even if you say that,

136
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:49,640
paying a salary to a robot cop?

137
00:08:50,180 --> 00:08:52,620
Give robots salaries and days off too!

138
00:08:52,620 --> 00:08:54,500
Treat them the same as humans!

139
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:56,560
That's unreasonable.

140
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:58,880
There's no precedent for that, either.

141
00:08:58,880 --> 00:09:02,380
Then at least create a department
just for independent robots!

142
00:09:02,380 --> 00:09:04,000
A robot police box, then!

143
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:06,380
I've had enough of being
worked to the bone by humans.

144
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:10,000
I understand how you feel,
but without a track record,

145
00:09:11,140 --> 00:09:12,780
then I'll go make one.

146
00:09:16,900 --> 00:09:19,080
And then it'll be a
robot police box, got it?

147
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:24,340
What a troublesome robot cop we've got here.

148
00:09:24,340 --> 00:09:25,140
Yes.

149
00:09:28,060 --> 00:09:29,320
That's how it is.

150
00:09:30,140 --> 00:09:31,480
Is that so?

151
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:33,460
A robot police box

152
00:09:33,460 --> 00:09:35,900
He comes up with the craziest ideas.

153
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:40,800
Yes.

154
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:42,840
Kameari Kōen-mae Police Box.

155
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:45,000
What, a case?

156
00:09:46,780 --> 00:09:48,460
Give me 500cc of milk.

157
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:49,380
Here you go.

158
00:09:51,300 --> 00:09:56,360
So if we just score a big win,
they'll set up a robot police box for us.

159
00:09:57,820 --> 00:09:59,600
And you'll be part of it too.

160
00:10:00,020 --> 00:10:00,400
Mm.

161
00:10:01,260 --> 00:10:02,460
Thank you for waiting.

162
00:10:03,100 --> 00:10:03,480
Right.

163
00:10:04,920 --> 00:10:06,160
That'll be 65 yen.

164
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:07,760
Yeah, yeah.

165
00:10:10,780 --> 00:10:12,820
Milk really is good after all.

166
00:10:16,820 --> 00:10:18,040
Looks like some kind of case.

167
00:10:18,580 --> 00:10:19,920
This is our chance to score a big win.

168
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:21,320
Keep up! Don't you dare lag behind!

169
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:22,020
Yes.

170
00:10:31,460 --> 00:10:34,560
Officers, hurry and bring him and a car!

171
00:10:35,360 --> 00:10:37,260
What a radical bunch!

172
00:10:37,660 --> 00:10:39,220
We can't get any closer like this.

173
00:10:40,060 --> 00:10:42,500
Chief, let's counterattack too!

174
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:43,500
No way.

175
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,920
That's a gunpowder factory, you know.

176
00:10:45,920 --> 00:10:48,580
And there are hostages inside, too.

177
00:10:49,280 --> 00:10:50,680
We can't just rashly move in.

178
00:10:51,260 --> 00:10:51,940
Damn it!

179
00:10:53,680 --> 00:10:54,800
So this is the scene

180
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:55,640
Yes, it is.

181
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:58,340
That's not allowed, Ennosuke.

182
00:10:58,840 --> 00:11:00,260
Leave this to us.

183
00:11:00,740 --> 00:11:02,760
They've got guns, you know.

184
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:05,560
No matter how many times I get shot,
I'll be fine.

185
00:11:05,560 --> 00:11:06,720
I'm a robot, after all.

186
00:11:07,120 --> 00:11:08,500
Are you an idiot?

187
00:11:08,500 --> 00:11:10,200
What do you mean, idiot?

188
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:15,120
Even if you're fine, what happens if the
hostages get shot, you defective robot?

189
00:11:16,660 --> 00:11:20,780
You said it again! A human, insulting
a robot like that, I won't forgive you!

190
00:11:20,780 --> 00:11:23,540
Please calm down, Ennosuke-san.

191
00:11:23,540 --> 00:11:25,940
Senpai, if you make him too angry...

192
00:11:28,260 --> 00:11:29,960
You bastard!

193
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:37,720
Don't come over here!

194
00:11:39,020 --> 00:11:40,560
It's awfully noisy in there.

195
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:42,340
Could the cash have arrived?

196
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:48,400
Stop!

197
00:11:48,400 --> 00:11:50,400
Do you not care what
happens to the hostages?

198
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:51,620
It's hot!

199
00:11:52,580 --> 00:11:53,920
Those eyes are dead serious.

200
00:11:53,920 --> 00:11:54,720
Run away!

201
00:12:01,520 --> 00:12:03,740
You idiot, don't go that way!

202
00:12:03,740 --> 00:12:04,440
Explosion!

203
00:12:04,440 --> 00:12:04,660
Matsuda!

204
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:08,000
Ennosuke-san!
There's a reservoir on the left!

205
00:12:08,220 --> 00:12:09,480
Please head that way!

206
00:12:11,680 --> 00:12:12,560
I'm going this way!

207
00:12:22,460 --> 00:12:23,340
Ennosuke!

208
00:12:23,740 --> 00:12:24,560
Ennosuke-san!

209
00:12:28,260 --> 00:12:29,560
It finally went out!

210
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:32,780
We did it!

211
00:12:35,480 --> 00:12:37,540
Now we've got our robot police box!

212
00:12:39,420 --> 00:12:41,020
That guy's got incredible luck.

213
00:12:42,120 --> 00:12:46,320
Thanks to robot officer prototype 005,

214
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:48,960
we were able to solve the case.

215
00:12:49,460 --> 00:12:51,680
Therefore, we hereby commend you.

216
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:53,980
Thank you.

217
00:12:54,840 --> 00:12:56,020
That's fine, but...

218
00:12:56,020 --> 00:12:59,020
You are going to build us
a robot police box, right?

219
00:12:59,900 --> 00:13:00,300
About that...

220
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:03,700
Are you planning to break your promise?

221
00:13:04,640 --> 00:13:06,680
Oh no, it's going to catch fire again!

222
00:13:07,160 --> 00:13:09,080
Don't make him angry, boss!

223
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:12,520
W-wait, I get it!

224
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:14,920
Let's build one for the robot deployment!

225
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:15,960
Yay!

226
00:13:16,620 --> 00:13:18,880
From now on,
I'm going to be out there kicking ass!

227
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:40,980
What do you mean by this, Chief?

228
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:44,900
Why is the robot police
box right next to ours?

229
00:13:45,420 --> 00:13:49,040
There was no other suitable land,
so it can't be helped.

230
00:13:49,040 --> 00:13:52,400
I'm heading to the station,
so don't slack off.

231
00:13:55,160 --> 00:13:57,960
Damn, the flame won't reach at all anymore.

232
00:13:58,420 --> 00:14:00,900
It's crept right up to within
a centimeter of the window!

233
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:03,360
Hey, Ennosuke!

234
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:08,200
What an amazing facility.

235
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:16,720
Well, are you surprised?

236
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:21,060
We've installed the latest technology,
fitting for a robot police box.

237
00:14:21,060 --> 00:14:23,720
What do you want, delinquent cop?

238
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:26,380
I came to complain, you defective robot.

239
00:14:26,380 --> 00:14:27,900
Who's the defective robot?

240
00:14:27,900 --> 00:14:30,740
You are, you defective piece of junk!

241
00:14:31,160 --> 00:14:32,040
What?!

242
00:14:33,280 --> 00:14:36,140
You dare talk back, you insolent human!

243
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:37,400
What?

244
00:14:38,620 --> 00:14:40,020
It's the lab on the second floor.

245
00:14:40,580 --> 00:14:42,020
What's wrong, Dame-Tarō?

246
00:14:43,780 --> 00:14:44,580
What is this?

247
00:14:44,580 --> 00:14:49,080
Sorry, the fuel spilled and it exploded.

248
00:14:49,620 --> 00:14:51,300
So that's his fuel?

249
00:14:51,300 --> 00:14:54,040
Yes, it's Development Unit 006.

250
00:14:54,620 --> 00:14:57,860
To remove abandoned bicycles
and illegally parked cars,

251
00:14:57,860 --> 00:14:59,700
we built a power robot.

252
00:15:00,740 --> 00:15:03,440
That was the plan,
but it still ended up this size

253
00:15:03,980 --> 00:15:07,500
Still, it's huge. Its body is sticking out!

254
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:12,040
Considering its strength and mobility,
it ended up this size...

255
00:15:12,660 --> 00:15:15,120
We were just about to do a test run.

256
00:15:20,940 --> 00:15:25,120
There's a cockpit in its chest, and it's
designed to be operated by two people.

257
00:15:25,760 --> 00:15:29,120
Sounds fun.
Let me take a turn at the controls too.

258
00:15:31,080 --> 00:15:32,300
Oi, wait up!

259
00:15:32,860 --> 00:15:34,940
Why are you getting in too?

260
00:15:34,940 --> 00:15:37,420
I'm not leaving it to a
delinquent cop like you.

261
00:15:37,900 --> 00:15:40,780
God, please turn the left wheel.

262
00:15:41,180 --> 00:15:42,460
That'll make it start moving.

263
00:15:42,460 --> 00:15:43,700
This one?

264
00:15:45,220 --> 00:15:47,440
It's like a classic car.

265
00:15:52,480 --> 00:15:53,440
The ceiling...

266
00:15:54,480 --> 00:15:56,940
Wow, it's standing up!

267
00:15:57,880 --> 00:15:59,680
Looks like it's easy to operate.

268
00:16:00,740 --> 00:16:01,600
Forward!

269
00:16:04,480 --> 00:16:06,080
That's a powerful movement.

270
00:16:06,720 --> 00:16:08,580
What kind of fuel does it use?

271
00:16:08,580 --> 00:16:09,960
It's nitro.

272
00:16:09,960 --> 00:16:10,880
Nitro?

273
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:15,620
Nitro, the stuff that blows up
from the slightest vibration?

274
00:16:15,620 --> 00:16:16,180
Yeah.

275
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:19,000
Why use something so dangerous?

276
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:21,060
Because it has the most power.

277
00:16:21,060 --> 00:16:22,220
You're kidding me.

278
00:16:22,220 --> 00:16:25,040
If the robot falls over, it'll blow up!

279
00:16:25,040 --> 00:16:26,220
Shut up already.

280
00:16:26,220 --> 00:16:28,660
As long as I don't mess up the controls,
it's fine.

281
00:16:28,660 --> 00:16:31,000
Your piloting? Like I'd trust that.

282
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:32,020
What did you say?

283
00:16:32,020 --> 00:16:35,480
Robots are far better pilots than humans!

284
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:37,520
No, no, hey, stop that!

285
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:39,920
If you catch fire, you'll explode!

286
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:41,020
I see.

287
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:43,540
I'm not riding this dangerous thing!

288
00:16:43,540 --> 00:16:44,720
I'm getting off.

289
00:16:46,680 --> 00:16:47,480
What's wrong?

290
00:16:47,480 --> 00:16:48,760
It won't open!

291
00:16:48,760 --> 00:16:49,700
What did you say?

292
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:54,540
Where are you going, god?

293
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,940
That way is the road!

294
00:16:59,080 --> 00:17:01,480
Damn you, are you making a fool of me?

295
00:17:02,460 --> 00:17:05,660
Wh-whoa, stop!
If you shake it, it'll explode!

296
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:15,860
W-what are you doing, god!

297
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:25,220
My robot police box!

298
00:17:26,520 --> 00:17:28,080
How dare you do this!

299
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:29,720
I didn't do anything.

300
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:30,640
Don't play dumb.

301
00:17:30,640 --> 00:17:32,620
Come on, calm down.

302
00:17:32,620 --> 00:17:34,240
Keep your cool.

303
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:41,720
The robot police box is...

304
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:47,960
Listen, it's gone out onto the road!

305
00:17:47,960 --> 00:17:48,500
What?

306
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:49,900
We have to stop it!

307
00:17:49,900 --> 00:17:51,040
I know that without you telling me.

308
00:17:51,040 --> 00:17:52,160
Stop!

309
00:17:56,220 --> 00:17:59,560
What are you doing?
Stop it already! I'm trying too!

310
00:17:59,560 --> 00:18:01,340
Shit, what's going on?

311
00:18:02,420 --> 00:18:05,340
Don't tell me the robot's moving on its own?

312
00:18:05,340 --> 00:18:06,380
What?

313
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:09,000
Give me a break, will you?

314
00:18:09,520 --> 00:18:10,880
Alright, hand over your license.

315
00:18:13,920 --> 00:18:15,740
Hey, stop that!

316
00:18:18,020 --> 00:18:19,380
What's that?

317
00:18:20,640 --> 00:18:22,060
Hey, stop!

318
00:18:22,060 --> 00:18:24,920
You there, robot! Stop!

319
00:18:26,360 --> 00:18:27,820
I told you to stop!

320
00:18:27,820 --> 00:18:30,180
Kankichi Ryotsu!

321
00:18:30,180 --> 00:18:32,120
What are you doing, you savage!

322
00:18:34,520 --> 00:18:36,400
Idiot! What have you done?

323
00:18:36,400 --> 00:18:39,600
Shut up!
I've been trying to stop it this whole time!

324
00:18:42,980 --> 00:18:45,880
You've really outdone yourself,
Kankichi Ryotsu.

325
00:18:49,380 --> 00:18:52,380
Reiko-san, what happened?

326
00:18:53,100 --> 00:18:57,380
I don't know.
I just got back and this is what's happened.

327
00:18:58,340 --> 00:19:00,140
What on earth...

328
00:19:02,160 --> 00:19:06,440
This is a Tyrannosaurus,
the strongest dinosaur on Earth.

329
00:19:07,280 --> 00:19:09,400
So it can't lose to any opponent?

330
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:11,040
Of course it can't.

331
00:19:27,700 --> 00:19:28,520
Looks like it started moving

332
00:19:39,740 --> 00:19:42,420
It's no good!
It's completely out of control!

333
00:19:42,780 --> 00:19:44,660
Stop it, even if we have to break it!

334
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:46,500
If I could, I'd have done it already!

335
00:19:46,900 --> 00:19:50,260
You bragged that it was smarter than humans,
you idiot!

336
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:52,280
What do you mean, idiot?!

337
00:19:53,740 --> 00:19:55,060
The fuel's catching fire!

338
00:19:55,060 --> 00:19:56,300
Aaaaaah!

339
00:19:56,300 --> 00:19:57,100
Aaaaaah!

340
00:19:57,100 --> 00:19:57,740
Aaaaaah!

341
00:19:57,740 --> 00:19:58,700
Aaaaaah!

342
00:19:58,700 --> 00:19:59,240
Aaaaaah!

343
00:19:59,240 --> 00:20:00,020
Aaaaaah!

344
00:20:00,020 --> 00:20:00,580
Aaaaaah!

345
00:20:01,060 --> 00:20:02,440
What is this robot?

346
00:20:02,440 --> 00:20:03,340
I'll remember that.

347
00:20:09,740 --> 00:20:10,760
Thank goodness.

348
00:20:12,860 --> 00:20:15,060
Lucky it landed in the river

349
00:20:16,540 --> 00:20:18,400
What's wrong? Why the funny face?

350
00:20:21,060 --> 00:20:22,520
Is that so? Pull yourself together.

351
00:20:22,520 --> 00:20:23,860
Keep your wits about you.

352
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:30,280
We're saved.

353
00:20:30,580 --> 00:20:36,060
Ahhh, that's exactly why humans are hopeless!
I don't want to hear that from you.

354
00:20:37,060 --> 00:20:47,600
Honestly, nothing good ever comes from being around this guy!
What? Senpai is piloting a giant robot and going berserk!

355
00:20:47,600 --> 00:20:55,600
They smashed our cars too... Ryo-chan!
Ohara-kun, what is the meaning of this?

356
00:20:56,300 --> 00:20:57,740
I have no idea either.

357
00:20:58,420 --> 00:21:03,340
Now that I think about it, he seemed to hold a major
grudge over being scolded by the chief last week.

358
00:21:04,760 --> 00:21:07,440
He did say he'd get revenge someday.

359
00:21:08,140 --> 00:21:11,720
Destroying the town over
something like that is unforgivable!

360
00:21:12,580 --> 00:21:16,380
Chief, trouble!
The giant robot is heading this way!

361
00:21:16,380 --> 00:21:16,940
What?

362
00:21:18,740 --> 00:21:22,540
Crap, at this rate it'll
crash into Katsushika Station!

363
00:21:22,540 --> 00:21:25,240
Oh no, that's bad! Stop it!

364
00:21:25,600 --> 00:21:28,140
That's why we've been struggling this whole time,
you idiot!

365
00:21:28,300 --> 00:21:30,040
- Circle around to the left with the F-Pa!
- Yes!

366
00:21:32,920 --> 00:21:34,240
Everyone at the station, right away!

367
00:21:34,820 --> 00:21:37,020
A giant robot is heading this way!

368
00:21:37,640 --> 00:21:40,080
All officers, form up and stop this thing!

369
00:21:41,340 --> 00:21:44,640
But Ryotsu, when did he even make a robot...

370
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:48,540
That's right! It looked like a robot
officer was riding along with him, though.

371
00:21:49,720 --> 00:21:52,560
I see! He had the robot officer build it!

372
00:21:53,660 --> 00:21:59,360
Ryotsu's scheming mind and the robot officer's
brains combined to create a devilish invention...

373
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:01,960
Now!

374
00:22:04,840 --> 00:22:07,160
Whatever it takes,
we have to stop it right here!

375
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:18,100
No good, the chains were dragged in too,
and it broke through.

376
00:22:18,860 --> 00:22:21,580
Damn it, isn't there any way to stop it?

377
00:22:22,640 --> 00:22:24,520
SS team, in position.

378
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:28,540
Once the robot comes within 30 meters,
you have permission to attack.

379
00:22:28,540 --> 00:22:29,180
Yes, sir!

380
00:22:29,440 --> 00:22:30,100
Chief!

381
00:22:30,920 --> 00:22:34,120
Now that it's come this far,
destroying the robot is our only option.

382
00:22:34,560 --> 00:22:37,460
If it goes well, the damage will be minimal.

383
00:22:38,060 --> 00:22:38,420
No way...

384
00:22:40,160 --> 00:22:40,960
Ryo-chan!

385
00:22:42,060 --> 00:22:42,900
Hey, how is it?!

386
00:22:44,440 --> 00:22:45,700
Alright, that's it, we're good.

387
00:22:46,280 --> 00:22:47,320
I cut the fuel.

388
00:22:47,320 --> 00:22:49,440
It'll stop after walking another 10 meters.

389
00:22:49,960 --> 00:22:51,020
Alright, good job!

390
00:22:52,560 --> 00:22:54,000
This should save Show

391
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:54,940
Eeeh?!

392
00:22:57,020 --> 00:22:58,960
Once it gets within another 10 meters, fire!

393
00:23:02,940 --> 00:23:04,440
Please stop!

394
00:23:04,580 --> 00:23:05,580
You can't do that!

395
00:23:05,920 --> 00:23:09,160
That robot runs on nitro!

396
00:23:09,420 --> 00:23:10,580
What?!

397
00:23:11,440 --> 00:23:13,940
Hey! Don't rush! You have to stop now!

398
00:23:14,120 --> 00:23:17,100
There's nitro inside the robot! Stop!

399
00:23:17,780 --> 00:23:18,460
Fire!

400
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:20,060
You idiot!

401
00:23:29,220 --> 00:23:30,880
The Katsushika Show is in full swing.

402
00:23:31,300 --> 00:23:33,800
But miraculously,
no one was hurt, apparently.

403
00:23:33,800 --> 00:23:35,680
Except for me, that is.

404
00:23:37,980 --> 00:23:39,220
Sorry, Ryo-chan.

405
00:23:39,220 --> 00:23:43,040
I never imagined the
robot would malfunction.

406
00:23:43,620 --> 00:23:44,960
I'm really sorry.

407
00:23:45,800 --> 00:23:49,880
Honestly, this is all because I
was stuck with that defective robot.

408
00:23:49,880 --> 00:23:52,660
What? Who are you calling a defective robot?

